    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="1226" n="1212" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00113 European War 1939/10–3044:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative on the Advisory Council for
                        Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-30T18:00:00+01:00">October 30, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 31—9:19 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>624. A note dated October 28 just received from Italian Prime Minister<anchor
                        n="79" xml:id="d750-f1"/> states that the competent Italian authorities have
                    taken steps for promoting the desequestration of property of British and
                    American subjects in Italy to point out to my Government that the Government of
                    Italy expects similar measures to be taken in the United States with regard to
                    Italian property still under sequestration. He requests any assurance which I
                    can give him in the matter.</p>
                <p>In this general connection the Italian Government was apprised by me some months
                    ago of the basis of treatment accorded to Italian property in the United States
                    insofar as was set forth in Department’s instruction No. 3 of May 25,
                        1944.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d750-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I should appreciate being informed as to what I should now say to President
                    Bonomi in reply to his note.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
